      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I\u0027d suggests returning std::pair\u003cint, float\u003e for a compound-result of both perecentage and number.\n\nIf you are fine with it, there are a couple of reasons I think the current approach works better.\n\n1. In the current architecture, PixelsDifferent is responsible for most of the heavy lifting of finding the pixels through the for loop. Having a percentage conversation in.\n\n2. IMO, having one function return both, it becomes less clear what the overall purpose is.\n\n3. If we have to do a `.first` and `.second`, anyone reading this would have to go back to the function, read it again and then see what first and second actually are, having PixelsDifferent() run to return pixels and that be converted to percentage would be cleaner in my opnion.\n\nIf there is another important reason/advantage for std::pair\u003c\u003e that I am missing, let me know.\n\nUnresolve if there is something I am missing here, otherwise you can merge this.",
